25
00:01:21,031 --> 00:01:29,966
Rym: But I saw something noteworthy, because I've never seen something like this before, on my bike home from work today, and I was not involved in this altercation.

26
00:01:30,367 --> 00:01:31,890
Rym: This was a long-.

27
00:01:31,970 --> 00:01:33,380
Scott: All you see is altercations.

28
00:01:33,602 --> 00:01:34,790
Scott: Don't you see anything nice?

29
00:01:35,951 --> 00:01:40,917
Rym: This is the first altercation I've seen in the year 2024 biking home.

30
00:01:42,178 --> 00:01:43,379
Rym: But it was a crazy one.

31
00:01:44,160 --> 00:01:52,970
Rym: So, biking home, I'm on an e-bike, one of those white ones, because now they have like a hundred of them next to Grand Central, and it's cheaper and faster than taking the subway home to take one of those home.

32
00:01:53,591 --> 00:01:55,533
Rym: So I'm riding against the Queensboro Bridge like normal.

33
00:01:55,693 --> 00:01:56,314
Rym: Everything's fine.

34
00:01:57,074 --> 00:02:01,159
Rym: And ahead of me are two kids who are also on the white e-bikes.

35
00:02:02,420 --> 00:02:03,802
Rym: They all go the same speed.

36
00:02:03,882 --> 00:02:05,063
Rym: Like, I can't overtake them.

37
00:02:05,664 --> 00:02:08,586
Rym: They couldn't get away from me if I were like chasing them or something.

38
00:02:08,866 --> 00:02:11,370
Rym: Those things go pretty much the same speed if you're pedaling.

39
00:02:13,090 --> 00:02:16,975
Rym: And I was biking up, and there's someone coming in the opposite direction.

40
00:02:17,556 --> 00:02:27,530
Rym: And as soon as he gets close to us, these two kids swerve out at him to try to run him off the trail like super aggressively, and he like swerves out of the way and falls over.

41
00:02:28,191 --> 00:02:29,972
Rym: And then they laugh and get back out of the bike lane.

42
00:02:30,413 --> 00:02:33,295
Rym: And then someone else is coming along the way, and they do the same thing to them.

43
00:02:33,676 --> 00:02:36,098
Rym: And then they swerve and like smack a pedestrian.

44
00:02:36,558 --> 00:02:49,250
Rym: And they basically just play chicken with every single person, bike, scooter, or pedestrian, who's coming the opposite direction, like yelling and slapping people, and like they cause a bunch of crashes along the way.

45
00:02:49,811 --> 00:02:53,338
Rym: And I'm like 50 feet behind them, and there's really nothing I can do.

46
00:02:53,578 --> 00:02:59,330
Rym: I just see this horrific tail play out, and then I get to the bottom of the bridge, and they head off down the road, and that's the end of that.

47
00:03:01,230 --> 00:03:01,832
Scott: I'm surprised.

48
00:03:01,852 --> 00:03:09,669
Scott: Like, if someone played chicken with me, and I could tell that it was on purpose and not just like, "Whoa, what's

49
00:03:09,829 --> 00:03:09,910
Scott: up?".

50
00:03:10,250 --> 00:03:18,710
Rym: There's definitely, for someone who's a skilled cyclist, if someone did that to me, and I believe you could do the same, I could ensure that they hit me in a way that harms them, but not me.

51
00:03:20,790 --> 00:03:31,468
Scott: Sure, but like, in that case, I would be like, you know, especially if it's a kid, it's like, yeah, I would probably violently assault them and say it was self-defense.

52
00:03:31,488 --> 00:03:32,149
Rym: They tried to kill me.

53
00:03:33,130 --> 00:03:39,530
Rym: People did yell and chase and try to go after them, but they couldn't catch them because they were on e-bikes, and they forced everyone off the road along the way.

54
00:03:42,451 --> 00:03:49,689
Scott: I guess I'd have to... I can't really picture exactly how this went down, that they played chicken with someone, but then kept going and didn't actually have to stop.

55
00:03:50,570 --> 00:03:58,510
Rym: Everyone either crashed, fell off their bike, swerved out of the way desperately to avoid them, and no one had the time to turn around.

56
00:03:58,630 --> 00:04:01,850
Scott: Oh, so they played chicken with them, and then at the last second, the kids pulled out of the way.

57
00:04:01,850 --> 00:04:02,954
Rym: No, the kids didn't pull out.

58
00:04:03,154 --> 00:04:07,489
Rym: Everyone else either swerved or got hit by them and fell over.

59
00:04:08,399 --> 00:04:08,523
Scott: I see.

60
00:04:08,992 --> 00:04:11,210
Rym: Yeah, like they knocked a bunch of people off their bikes.

61
00:04:11,910 --> 00:04:18,730
Scott: I see, so if it's clearly intentional, right, I'm just going to look... You know actually what I would do if I had enough time?

62
00:04:18,790 --> 00:04:26,850
Rym: Because I thought if I had been on my bike, I think I would have actually caught up to them and knocked one of them over just so consequences could happen.

63
00:04:26,950 --> 00:04:30,105
Rym: But I was on an e-bike that literally cannot go faster than that.

64
00:04:30,346 --> 00:04:31,170
Rym: All I could do was watch.

65
00:04:32,191 --> 00:04:38,590
Scott: I think, I don't know, I guess if someone's playing chicken with me, and I can tell, but it's not that they don't see me.

66
00:04:38,750 --> 00:04:44,170
Scott: That they're like trying to play chicken like an idiot, and they still refuse to get out of the way.

67
00:04:44,890 --> 00:04:49,030
Scott: It's like, you know, once they're past me, my chances is going to be gone.

68
00:04:50,731 --> 00:04:56,010
Scott: If I have enough time, I think I could like hop off, and then give them, and then shove them down.

69
00:04:56,550 --> 00:04:58,009
Rym: So there was a moment, there was a jogger.

70
00:04:58,190 --> 00:05:03,310
Scott: So I could hop off before they hit me, and then just like, you know, take them out.

71
00:05:03,570 --> 00:05:07,369
Rym: The jogger guy, they like, the one kid like hit him hard enough to knock him over.

72
00:05:09,435 --> 00:05:10,490
Rym: And they like, they slowed down.

73
00:05:10,711 --> 00:05:12,137
Scott: Wait, so the guy was jogging.

74
00:05:12,217 --> 00:05:15,010
Scott: If he's jogging, yeah, he definitely could have pushed the kid over.

75
00:05:15,290 --> 00:05:17,969
Rym: I don't think he thought the kid was actually going to ram him.

76
00:05:18,290 --> 00:05:19,910
Scott: Yeah, he didn't realize what was happening.

77
00:05:20,110 --> 00:05:25,570
Scott: Because I would not assume that a kid would... In your position, you could have yelled at the people coming the other way.

78
00:05:25,630 --> 00:05:30,010
Rym: No, I was trying to warn everyone along the way, but no one... Think about it, think about New Yorkers.

79
00:05:30,852 --> 00:05:32,569
Rym: If someone's yelling, you kind of just ignore them.

80
00:05:33,810 --> 00:05:39,230
Scott: I guess, but it's like, you know, that kid's going to hit you with his bike, attack him, stop him, right?

81
00:05:39,372 --> 00:05:40,370
Scott: I'd be like, oh shit.

82
00:05:40,730 --> 00:05:44,030
Rym: Yeah, but imagine you're doing your thing, and someone yells, attack that kid.

83
00:05:46,572 --> 00:05:51,571
Scott: I guess you could have yelled something like, I guess, you know, hindsight is 20/20.

84
00:05:51,571 --> 00:05:54,210
Rym: I couldn't yell much else other than watch out, out of the way.

85
00:05:55,012 --> 00:05:57,249
Scott: You could be like, he stole my phone, stop him, right?

86
00:05:58,555 --> 00:06:00,230
Scott: And people would if you did that, right?

87
00:06:00,511 --> 00:06:06,710
Scott: In New York, if you're like, that guy stole that lady's purse, everyone around would be like, you know, get him, right?

88
00:06:06,870 --> 00:06:06,966
Rym: Yeah.

89
00:06:08,112 --> 00:06:10,810
Scott: They wouldn't do it if it was like, that guy's shoplifting, who gives a shit?

90
00:06:10,870 --> 00:06:13,550
Scott: But it's like, that guy stole someone's phone, he's got someone's purse, stop him.

91
00:06:13,550 --> 00:06:19,390
Rym: I mean, one time, years ago, I was walking down toward the 7 train, and a kid like slams into me.

92
00:06:19,450 --> 00:06:23,829
Rym: This kid was like 13 or 14, he slams into me, and I was like, before I could even react, he runs off.

93
00:06:24,332 --> 00:06:28,149
Rym: And then like 10 seconds later, two cops come running, and they yell, where'd he go?

94
00:06:28,712 --> 00:06:31,030
Rym: And I didn't say shit, and neither did anyone else.

95
00:06:32,592 --> 00:06:34,710
Scott: Yeah, that's a totally different situation, right?

96
00:06:34,770 --> 00:06:40,170
Scott: Because if New Yorker, like if someone steals a phone, and New Yorkers stop him, right?

97
00:06:40,337 --> 00:06:40,490
Scott: Yeah.

98
00:06:40,790 --> 00:06:46,330
Scott: It's going to be like, take the phone back, give it back to the person it belongs to, and then get the fuck out of here, asshole, right?

99
00:06:47,151 --> 00:06:49,250
Scott: Right, that's the right solution, and you know what?

100
00:06:49,330 --> 00:06:51,104
Scott: That's what police should fucking do, right?

101
00:06:51,910 --> 00:07:01,350
Scott: You don't need to arrest someone who's clearly, like, their life is ruined, and if you arrest them and go through all the justice system, you're just costing us and them a lot of pain and hassle.

102
00:07:01,550 --> 00:07:03,562
Scott: All we want is the fucking phone back, right?

103
00:07:03,642 --> 00:07:04,950
Scott: Repair the damage, right?

104
00:07:05,591 --> 00:07:07,368
Scott: That's what you gotta do, right?

105
00:07:08,872 --> 00:07:12,069
Scott: So it's like, did we need these kids to go to jail, or, right?

106
00:07:12,390 --> 00:07:14,510
Scott: No, we just need them to learn their fucking lesson, right?

107
00:07:14,635 --> 00:07:14,702
Scott: Yep.

108
00:07:14,770 --> 00:07:18,410
Scott: Someone pushes them over one time, they won't do that shit again, right?

109
00:07:19,450 --> 00:07:23,890
Scott: I bet you all those stupid kids doing the subway surfing, right?

110
00:07:24,350 --> 00:07:29,190
Scott: Yeah, there are kids out there probably still doing the subway surfing, but not the ones who saw a friend die.

111
00:07:30,310 --> 00:07:31,550
Rym: Yep, or maybe they are.

112
00:07:31,550 --> 00:07:36,450
Scott: If you saw your friend die subway surfing, and you're still doing it, you should be allowed to do it, because you don't have a job.

113
00:07:36,470 --> 00:07:41,827
Rym: Yeah, and if you fully understand the consequences, and it's a thing that won't hurt someone else...

114
00:07:42,991 --> 00:07:45,609
Scott: Right, well just leave your corpse on the tracks, you know?

115
00:07:46,433 --> 00:07:46,968
Scott: Okay, bro.

116
00:07:47,991 --> 00:07:54,470
Rym: So yeah, I'm not gonna just tell random bike anecdotes anymore, because I think I've covered every possible thing, but this was a new one for me.

117
00:07:55,431 --> 00:08:00,330
Rym: And it doesn't take that long to get over that bridge, so it wasn't like there was a long time to interact with this situation.

118
00:08:01,270 --> 00:08:02,703
Scott: Yeah, I don't know.

119
00:08:02,763 --> 00:08:03,349
Scott: It's a new one.

120
00:08:03,950 --> 00:08:13,490
