Scott: It always has, but even back in the Harryhausen days, but, uh, it's still a huge pain in the ass and the, and is expensive and time consuming, which is why Pokemon concierge is so short.

388
00:28:48,401 --> 00:28:49,224
Rym: Yep.

389
00:28:49,224 --> 00:28:50,891
Rym: 15 to 20 minutes is the running time for this thing.

390
00:28:50,911 --> 00:28:52,699
Rym: There's only four episodes of the first season.

391
00:28:53,281 --> 00:28:53,401
Scott: Right.

392
00:28:53,421 --> 00:29:03,038
Scott: And the Pokemon and the Pinocchio, which is just one movie, uh, was, you know, very expensive, but, uh, if I had to say the most like in terms of only 117 minutes.

393
00:29:04,300 --> 00:29:09,847
Rym: So the thing about Pokemon concierge that they got, they like 100% right is?

394
00:29:10,187 --> 00:29:12,971
Rym: it centers the Pokemon and the Pokemon.

395
00:29:13,211 --> 00:29:18,277
Rym: Like this is just an excuse to see amazing stop motion of Pokemon that you like.

396
00:29:18,498 --> 00:29:20,280
Rym: Like the Pokemon are so good.

397
00:29:20,941 --> 00:29:22,002
Scott: I think it's different than that.

398
00:29:22,082 --> 00:29:28,588
Scott: I think it's an excuse to make you like Pokemon for the audience.

399
00:29:28,708 --> 00:29:28,948
Scott: Right?

400
00:29:28,988 --> 00:29:33,893
Scott: So it's like, even if you don't know about Pokemon or care about Pokemon, right?

401
00:29:33,953 --> 00:29:37,216
Scott: It's about basically this Island resort, right?

402
00:29:37,356 --> 00:29:40,940
Scott: Where Pokemon go on vacation, not people.

403
00:29:41,260 --> 00:29:41,461
Rym: Yep.

404
00:29:42,021 --> 00:29:46,387
Scott: And there are both people and Pokemon that work there taking care of the Pokemon.

405
00:29:47,248 --> 00:29:56,820
Scott: And this one person is escaping their boring corporate life of overwork, uh, to go become a concierge at this resort.

406
00:29:57,541 --> 00:30:00,843
Rym: You know, if that were an option, uh, I'd be there right now.

407
00:30:01,463 --> 00:30:01,784
Scott: Of course.

408
00:30:01,804 --> 00:30:01,984
Scott: Right.

409
00:30:02,024 --> 00:30:02,825
Scott: So you'd be fighting.

410
00:30:02,845 --> 00:30:04,446
Scott: That would be the hardest job in the world to get.

411
00:30:05,246 --> 00:30:09,650
Scott: But, uh, them getting the job right.

412
00:30:09,770 --> 00:30:12,332
Scott: And, and having their life refreshed, right.

413
00:30:12,612 --> 00:30:15,334
Scott: Is sort of what the show does for the audience, right?

414
00:30:15,394 --> 00:30:23,300
Scott: Is you escape from your daily drudgery to the magical Pokemon Island where Pokemon are just chilling and having a good time.

415
00:30:23,440 --> 00:30:29,750
Rym: I mean, it's pretty on the nose when there's a moment in the show where she's like, she sees a Pokemon evolve, which it's a good episode.

416
00:30:29,771 --> 00:30:30,351
Rym: I mean, they're all good.

417
00:30:30,372 --> 00:30:33,497
Rym: There's only four, but she's like, man, I wish I could evolve.

418
00:30:33,777 --> 00:30:34,378
Rym: I wish I could.

419
00:30:34,418 --> 00:30:35,500
Scott: You literally just did.

420
00:30:35,620 --> 00:30:35,920
Rym: Yup.

421
00:30:37,702 --> 00:30:57,200
Scott: Um, but it's like, yeah, even if your favorite Pokemon doesn't appear in this show, even if you hate all the Pokemon that are in the show, it's like you sort of, you know, it's just animals having a good time interacting and, you know, bringing joy to the characters around them, but also to the audience watching.

422
00:30:57,260 --> 00:30:57,440
Scott: Right.

423
00:30:57,460 --> 00:31:00,684
Rym: I mean, animals having a good time is a genre of internet content.

424
00:31:01,365 --> 00:31:01,526
Scott: Right.

425
00:31:01,546 --> 00:31:04,169
Scott: It's like, you think about it, like people just go watch cat videos.

426
00:31:04,189 --> 00:31:11,219
Scott: This is like someone making cat video, except it's Psyduck video instead on purpose.

427
00:31:11,680 --> 00:31:11,840
Scott: Right.

428
00:31:12,601 --> 00:31:19,428
Rym: And I think they understood the mission in that the voice cast is four people because it's pretty much all Pokemon.

429
00:31:20,449 --> 00:31:20,849
Scott: Pretty much.

430
00:31:22,010 --> 00:31:29,638
Scott: Um, but yeah, it's like, it's funny how the main Pokemon in the show, which is Psyduck, uh, which you should, I imagine you know that already.

431
00:31:29,678 --> 00:31:31,420
Rym: Top tier Pokemon that Psyduck.

432
00:31:31,500 --> 00:31:31,700
Rym: Right.

433
00:31:32,101 --> 00:31:36,285
Scott: It's a Pokemon that it's like, you know, Psyduck, but do I care about that?

434
00:31:36,326 --> 00:31:36,766
Scott: Not really.

435
00:31:36,786 --> 00:31:38,428
Scott: I would never had a Psyduck in my team.

436
00:31:38,808 --> 00:31:39,910
Scott: I never cared about him.

437
00:31:40,050 --> 00:31:44,074
Rym: I only like Psyduck because of Psyducks side plots in the original cartoon.

438
00:31:44,735 --> 00:31:44,935
Scott: Right.

439
00:31:45,276 --> 00:31:48,820
Scott: But here, this show, like it makes you like the Psyduck.

440
00:31:51,100 --> 00:31:56,946
Scott: Um, you know, it's like, they don't need to do a fan service of giving you what you want.

441
00:31:57,006 --> 00:32:05,615
Scott: It's like they, it's, it's so, uh, endearing that they can, you know, make you like what they want you to like and then give you that.

442
00:32:05,856 --> 00:32:05,976
Scott: Right.

443
00:32:06,036 --> 00:32:09,740
Scott: It's like they can change your taste and then give you the food they just made you like.

444
00:32:11,040 --> 00:32:14,483
Scott: Rather, rather than trying to figure out the food you like and trying to find it.

445
00:32:14,823 --> 00:32:18,886
Rym: But I think that's also a big key because this is the kind of show where someone's never heard of Pokemon.

446
00:32:18,906 --> 00:32:20,507
Rym: They'll probably find it delightful.

447
00:32:20,827 --> 00:32:25,490
Rym: If someone's a mega Pokemon fan, they're going to love it for a lot of other reasons.

448
00:32:25,670 --> 00:32:30,033
Rym: Like I can't imagine who would not enjoy the show, especially considering how short it is.

449
00:32:30,874 --> 00:32:33,736
Scott: A cold, dark and evil human being.

450
00:32:33,776 --> 00:32:35,497
Rym: I don't think many Republicans would like this show.

451
00:32:36,118 --> 00:32:39,540
Scott: I don't know, but even they might, you know, might like it.

452
00:32:39,660 --> 00:32:40,161
Rym: I hope so.

453
00:32:40,381 --> 00:32:42,503
Scott: That's, that's how you turn someone from the path of evil.

454
00:32:43,063 --> 00:32:45,946
Scott: What do they find in here that is not to like?

455
00:32:47,748 --> 00:32:51,551
Scott: It's literally just people going to an island and having a good time.

456
00:32:51,852 --> 00:32:52,132
Scott: Right.

457
00:32:52,152 --> 00:32:56,316
Scott: Doing everyday in somewhat not everyday stuff with Pokemon involved.

458
00:32:57,517 --> 00:33:00,320
Rym: It's very, it's everyday stuff for the Pokemon universe, I would say.

459
00:33:01,240 --> 00:33:01,440
Scott: Yeah.

460
00:33:01,821 --> 00:33:02,221
Scott: Yeah.

461
00:33:02,422 --> 00:33:08,549
Scott: Try it on clothes, exercising, dancing, swimming, flying.

462
00:33:08,909 --> 00:33:09,109
Rym: Yep.

463
00:33:09,630 --> 00:33:10,831
Rym: And there is good news.

464
00:33:10,931 --> 00:33:18,540
Rym: if you, cause like if you're a geek, if you listen to GeekNights, there's no reason not to watch this unless you don't have Netflix and you don't have Netflix either.

465
00:33:18,780 --> 00:33:19,661
Rym: Yarr!

466
00:33:19,841 --> 00:33:25,646
Rym: Either Yarr or whenever you rotate Netflix in to catch up on shows, this is just four episodes.

467
00:33:25,726 --> 00:33:29,630
Rym: And while there is a new season that has been ordered, that is official.

468
00:33:29,650 --> 00:33:31,251
Scott: It's going to take a while.

469
00:33:31,371 --> 00:33:32,552
Rym: It's going to take a while.

470
00:33:32,612 --> 00:33:35,075
Rym: They only announced it a couple months ago that it was coming.

471
00:33:35,535 --> 00:33:41,240
Rym: And I can't imagine they're going to make more than like four or five more episodes at a time considering.

472
00:33:41,881 --> 00:33:45,504
Rym: So everyone should watch this.

473
00:33:45,904 --> 00:33:55,132
Rym: And especially if you're stressed about the world right now, I can think of at least seven things that it is perfectly normal to be stressed about right now in the real world.

474
00:33:55,172 --> 00:33:58,015
Rym: Just off the top of my head that are extremely worrying.

475
00:33:58,716 --> 00:34:03,600
Rym: This is a show that I think you could enjoy and maybe stop thinking about those things for a little while.

476
00:34:04,141 --> 00:34:09,467
Scott: And you can also, I think another thing is that because it's so short, this is the kind of thing you can go back to.

477
00:34:09,708 --> 00:34:10,047
Rym: Oh yeah.

478
00:34:10,549 --> 00:34:13,933
Scott: You know, even though it's short, right, you think, ah, I finished it already.

479
00:34:14,353 --> 00:34:15,534
Scott: Why not watch it again?

480
00:34:15,554 --> 00:34:19,120
Scott: It's like, it'll only take you, you know, an hour.

481
00:34:20,600 --> 00:34:30,034
Rym: This is the kind of show where like if we're hanging out with some friends at a place like at their apartment or at a convention and someone's like, oh, I haven't seen Pokemon Casio.

