494
00:35:31,901 --> 00:35:42,500
Rym: But in the last several GeekNights episodes, a theme emerged kind of like, uh, kind of like, uh, the Graybles from Adventure Time by the end of the episode.

495
00:35:42,660 --> 00:35:53,500
Rym: Like in this episode, I've had, we had, the theme, a theme that emerged from multiple things we talked about was around caring about what happens versus something else in media.

496
00:35:54,422 --> 00:35:58,279
Scott: Yeah, that's the thing I've been on for a year or a few.

497
00:35:59,781 --> 00:36:07,840
Scott: I like abstract, I realized, you know, some time ago, it's like, I like abstract arts a lot more than non-abstract arts.

498
00:36:10,124 --> 00:36:16,360
Scott: And yet the mass media in our society seems to mostly be concentrating on the exact opposite of abstract arts.

499
00:36:16,640 --> 00:36:16,700
Rym: Yup.

500
00:36:17,061 --> 00:36:25,620
Rym: I mean, case in point, what's better, a giant space baby and then question mark or here's how the guy got back from Mars in full detail credits.

501
00:36:26,423 --> 00:36:26,663
Scott: Yup.

502
00:36:28,409 --> 00:36:28,891
Scott: The first one.

503
00:36:29,854 --> 00:36:30,637
Scott: By a lot.

504
00:36:31,178 --> 00:36:31,640
Scott: Landside.

